{
  "name": "lsm-tree",
  "description": "A high-performance Log-Structured Merge Tree (LSMT) implementation in Rust designed as a modular storage primitive for key-value engines. It features block-based SSTables with partitioned indexes, Bloom filters for optimized point lookups, and diverse compaction strategies including Leveled, Size-Tiered, and FIFO. The architecture supports MVCC via snapshots, multi-threaded memtable flushing, and optional key-value separation to mitigate write amplification in blob-heavy workloads.",
